# The Rust image builds from the repo root; send only what it compiles.
*
!backend-rs/Cargo.toml
!backend-rs/Cargo.lock
!backend-rs/src
# sqlx::migrate!() embeds these at compile time, so they must reach the build
# context. Without this line the COPY fails with "/backend-rs/migrations": not
# found -- the file is committed, it just never arrives.
!backend-rs/migrations
# Every game's data file is read at COMPILE time with include_str!, from the
# same copy the Python reads, so each one must reach the build context too.
# Miss one and the build fails with "couldn't read ...: No such file or
# directory" from rustc, not from COPY -- which is why the three that were
# already here did not hint at the two that were not.
!backend/app/kart_tracks.json
!backend/app/platformer_levels.json
!backend/app/fps_map.json
!backend/app/golf_courses.json
!backend/app/strike_map.json
!backend/app/data/pokemon.json
